SUMMARY:Keith Karnaky Jazz Group at Archway Gallery
DESCRIPTION:Now celebrating its fiftieth year\, the member-owned Montrose gallery audience presents an evening of timeless jazz by audience favorite Keith Karnaky—joined by an ensemble of top improvisational musicians. \nThe program will feature timeless jazz standards and improvisations in one of Houston’s most intimate listening spaces. \nKarnaky will be joined by acclaimed saxophonist Woody Witt—an internationally recognized performer\, composer\, and educator\, with a career spanning jazz and classical music. \nOpened in 1976\, Archway Gallery is currently celebrating its fiftieth year. \nAdmission\nFree. Learn more. \nAcclaimed Saxophonist Woody Witt joins Keith Karnaky for a night of live timeless jazz songs at Archway Gallery. | Photo courtesy of Archway Gallery \n \nThis Featured Calendar Listing was sponsored by the event organizer and boosted in our calendar with images and more details. \nLearn more about promoting your event\, organization\, business\, or offer across all of our channels.
URL:https://365thingsinhouston.com/calendar/road-trips-opening-reception-at-archway-gallery-august-2026/
LOCATION:Archway Gallery\, 2305 Dunlavy St\, Houston\, TX\, 77006\, United States
